    "created_at": "2025-02-25T04:06:59Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-02-25T04:06:59Z",
    "body": "Sure, it's just not clear that this particular algorithm represents the relevant process hop. It's called from three very different call sites, all of which appear to be way after the initial step that goes in parallel.\n\nIf we wanted to be more disciplined about snapshotting, I guess we would add _initiatorPolicyContainer_ and _parentPolicyContainer_ to the source and target snapshot params, respectively, before we go in parallel. _responsePolicyContainer_ comes from the network so I don't think it can change; cloning it is probably not necessary. _historyPolicyContainer_ is presumably stored in the browser process. Should it be cloned?\n\nI guess this would all be a lot clearer if we knew which parts of the policy container were mutable, if any. I guess CSP, due to `<meta>`? Anything else?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
